{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lq89QN3eXT66rXoHh1ipZH","type":"tool_result","content":"5:> For the best experience, use **[Remote Notion MCP](https://developers.notion.com/docs/mcp)**,\n9:> **faster results using far fewer tokens**.\n13:> time waiting, less context-window usage, and lower token costs. It also uses OAuth\n15:> tokens, JSON configuration, manual page sharing, or a local server to maintain.\n20:> | **Token-efficient responses** | ✅ | Limited |\n25:> | Seamless OAuth setup | ✅ | Manual token and JSON configuration |\n29:> Learn more and get started in the [Remote Notion MCP documentation](https://developers.notion.com/docs/mcp).\n37:![notion-mcp-sm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c07003c-8455-4636-b298-d60ffdf46cd8)\n39:This project implements an [MCP server](https://spec.modelcontextprotocol.io/) for the [Notion API](https://developers.notion.com/reference/intro).\n41:![mcp-demo](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3ff90a7-7801-48a9-b807-f7dd47f0d3d6)\n93:The server exposes two tools for working with page content as enhanced Markdown instead of block JSON, which is significantly more token-efficient for AI agents:\n106:Go to [https://www.notion.so/profile/integrations](https://www.notion.so/profile/integrations) and create a new **internal** integration or select an existing one.\n108:![Creating a Notion Integration token](docs/images/integrations-creation.png)\n112:For example, you can create a read-only integration token by giving only \"Read content\" access from the \"Configuration\" tab:\n114:![Notion Integration Token Capabilities showing Read content checked](docs/images/integrations-capabilities.png)\n128:![Adding Integration Token to Notion Connections](docs/images/connections.png)\n138:###### Option 1: Using NOTION_TOKEN (recommended)\n147:        \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"ntn_****\"\n163:        \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS\": \"{\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\", \\\"Notion-Version\\\": \\\"2025-09-03\\\" }\"\n182:          \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS\": \"{\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\", \\\"Notion-Version\\\": \\\"2025-09-03\\\" }\"\n208:        \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"ntn_****\"\n215:For more information, see the [Copilot CLI documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/about-copilot-cli).\n225:Using NOTION_TOKEN (recommended):\n236:        \"-e\", \"NOTION_TOKEN\",\n240:        \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"ntn_****\"\n262:        \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS\": \"{\\\"Authorization\\\":\\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\",\\\"Notion-Version\\\":\\\"2025-09-03\\\"}\"\n285:Using NOTION_TOKEN (recommended):\n297:        \"NOTION_TOKEN=ntn_****\",\n317:        \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS={\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\", \\\"Notion-Version\\\": \\\"2025-09-03\\\"}\",\n327:![Copying your Integration token from the Configuration tab in the developer portal](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/67b44536-5333-49fa-809c-59581bf5370a)\n345:#### Streamable HTTP transport\n347:For web-based applications or clients that prefer HTTP communication, you can use the Streamable HTTP transport:\n350:# Run with Streamable HTTP transport on port 3000 (default)\n351:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http\n354:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --port 8080\n357:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --host 0.0.0.0\n359:# Run with a custom authentication token\n360:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --auth-token \"your-secret-token\"\n363:When using Streamable HTTP transport, the server will be available at `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp` by default.\n365:##### Authentication\n367:The Streamable HTTP transport requires bearer token authentication for security. You have three options:\n369:###### Option 1: Auto-generated token (only for development)\n372:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http\n375:The server will generate a secure random token and write it to a file with restricted permissions:\n378:Generated auth token written to: /tmp/.notion-mcp-auth-token-12345\n381:###### Option 2: Custom token via command line (recommended for production)\n384:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --auth-token \"your-secret-token\"\n387:###### Option 3: Custom token via environment variable (recommended for production)\n390:AUTH_TOKEN=\"your-secret-token\" npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http\n393:The command line argument `--auth-token` takes precedence over the `AUTH_TOKEN` environment variable if both are provided.\n395:###### Unsafe option: disable HTTP authentication\n397:You can disable bearer token authentication only with the explicit unsafe flag:\n400:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --unsafe-disable-auth\n403:WARNING: `--unsafe-disable-auth` is unsafe. The server may be reachable to pages you visit via DNS rebinding. Only use it on an isolated network.\n405:When authentication is disabled, the server enables DNS rebinding protection by checking the `Host` and `Origin` headers against the configured local host and loopback hosts. The previous `--disable-auth` flag is still accepted as a deprecated alias, but it will print a warning.\n407:##### Making HTTP requests\n409:All requests to the Streamable HTTP transport must include the bearer token in the Authorization header:\n413:curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer your-token-here\" \\\n417:     http://localhost:3000/mcp\n420:**Note:** Make sure to set either the `NOTION_TOKEN` environment variable (recommended) or the `OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS` environment variable with your Notion integration token when using either transport mode.\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 60]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37fb73b0-c435-4c14-8aa8-60d6fbf1b4a4","uuid":"1062373f-f9c1-45f3-8af6-475d19d1dd7c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:19:03.839Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"5:> For the best experience, use **[Remote Notion MCP](https://developers.notion.com/docs/mcp)**,\n9:> **faster results using far fewer tokens**.\n13:> time waiting, less context-window usage, and lower token costs. It also uses OAuth\n15:> tokens, JSON configuration, manual page sharing, or a local server to maintain.\n20:> | **Token-efficient responses** | ✅ | Limited |\n25:> | Seamless OAuth setup | ✅ | Manual token and JSON configuration |\n29:> Learn more and get started in the [Remote Notion MCP documentation](https://developers.notion.com/docs/mcp).\n37:![notion-mcp-sm](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6c07003c-8455-4636-b298-d60ffdf46cd8)\n39:This project implements an [MCP server](https://spec.modelcontextprotocol.io/) for the [Notion API](https://developers.notion.com/reference/intro).\n41:![mcp-demo](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e3ff90a7-7801-48a9-b807-f7dd47f0d3d6)\n93:The server exposes two tools for working with page content as enhanced Markdown instead of block JSON, which is significantly more token-efficient for AI agents:\n106:Go to [https://www.notion.so/profile/integrations](https://www.notion.so/profile/integrations) and create a new **internal** integration or select an existing one.\n108:![Creating a Notion Integration token](docs/images/integrations-creation.png)\n112:For example, you can create a read-only integration token by giving only \"Read content\" access from the \"Configuration\" tab:\n114:![Notion Integration Token Capabilities showing Read content checked](docs/images/integrations-capabilities.png)\n128:![Adding Integration Token to Notion Connections](docs/images/connections.png)\n138:###### Option 1: Using NOTION_TOKEN (recommended)\n147:        \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"ntn_****\"\n163:        \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS\": \"{\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\", \\\"Notion-Version\\\": \\\"2025-09-03\\\" }\"\n182:          \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS\": \"{\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\", \\\"Notion-Version\\\": \\\"2025-09-03\\\" }\"\n208:        \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"ntn_****\"\n215:For more information, see the [Copilot CLI documentation](https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/about-copilot-cli).\n225:Using NOTION_TOKEN (recommended):\n236:        \"-e\", \"NOTION_TOKEN\",\n240:        \"NOTION_TOKEN\": \"ntn_****\"\n262:        \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS\": \"{\\\"Authorization\\\":\\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\",\\\"Notion-Version\\\":\\\"2025-09-03\\\"}\"\n285:Using NOTION_TOKEN (recommended):\n297:        \"NOTION_TOKEN=ntn_****\",\n317:        \"OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS={\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer ntn_****\\\", \\\"Notion-Version\\\": \\\"2025-09-03\\\"}\",\n327:![Copying your Integration token from the Configuration tab in the developer portal](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/67b44536-5333-49fa-809c-59581bf5370a)\n345:#### Streamable HTTP transport\n347:For web-based applications or clients that prefer HTTP communication, you can use the Streamable HTTP transport:\n350:# Run with Streamable HTTP transport on port 3000 (default)\n351:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http\n354:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --port 8080\n357:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --host 0.0.0.0\n359:# Run with a custom authentication token\n360:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --auth-token \"your-secret-token\"\n363:When using Streamable HTTP transport, the server will be available at `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/mcp` by default.\n365:##### Authentication\n367:The Streamable HTTP transport requires bearer token authentication for security. You have three options:\n369:###### Option 1: Auto-generated token (only for development)\n372:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http\n375:The server will generate a secure random token and write it to a file with restricted permissions:\n378:Generated auth token written to: /tmp/.notion-mcp-auth-token-12345\n381:###### Option 2: Custom token via command line (recommended for production)\n384:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --auth-token \"your-secret-token\"\n387:###### Option 3: Custom token via environment variable (recommended for production)\n390:AUTH_TOKEN=\"your-secret-token\" npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http\n393:The command line argument `--auth-token` takes precedence over the `AUTH_TOKEN` environment variable if both are provided.\n395:###### Unsafe option: disable HTTP authentication\n397:You can disable bearer token authentication only with the explicit unsafe flag:\n400:npx @notionhq/notion-mcp-server --transport http --unsafe-disable-auth\n403:WARNING: `--unsafe-disable-auth` is unsafe. The server may be reachable to pages you visit via DNS rebinding. Only use it on an isolated network.\n405:When authentication is disabled, the server enables DNS rebinding protection by checking the `Host` and `Origin` headers against the configured local host and loopback hosts. The previous `--disable-auth` flag is still accepted as a deprecated alias, but it will print a warning.\n407:##### Making HTTP requests\n409:All requests to the Streamable HTTP transport must include the bearer token in the Authorization header:\n413:curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer your-token-here\" \\\n417:     http://localhost:3000/mcp\n420:**Note:** Make sure to set either the `NOTION_TOKEN` environment variable (recommended) or the `OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS` environment variable with your Notion integration token when using either transport mode.","numLines":60,"totalLines":86,"appliedLimit":60},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Lq89QN3eXT66rXoHh1ipZH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
